----------------------------------------Command Line Basics--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The command line allows you to interact with Linux using commands instead of a graphical interface.

Basic syntax:
command [options] [arguments]

Example:
ls -l /home
ls       → command
-l       → option
/home    → argument
Get help
man command

Example:
man ls

Short help:
command --help

Example:
ls --help
Clear terminal
clear

or:

Ctrl + L
Show current user
whoami
Show command location
which command

Example:
which python

