5. Key Operators
Linux uses operators to combine and control commands.

> Redirect output
ls > files.txt

Creates/overwrites files.txt.

>> Append output
ls >> files.txt

Adds output to the end of the file.
< Input redirection
command < file.txt

Uses the file as input.
| Pipe

Sends the output of one command to another command.
ls -l | grep ".txt"

Example:
ls -l
  ↓
grep ".txt"
&&

Run the second command only if the first succeeds.
mkdir test && cd test
||

Run the second command if the first command fails.
cd test || mkdir test
;

Run commands regardless of whether the previous command succeeds.

pwd; ls; whoami
&

Run a command in the background.
command &

