6. Viewing and Displaying Files

Display entire file
cat file.txt

Display file with line numbers
cat -n file.txt

View the beginning of a file
head file.txt

Specify number of lines:
head -n 20 file.txt

View the end of a file
tail file.txt

Specify number of lines:
tail -n 20 file.txt

Monitor a file in real time
tail -f /var/log/syslog

This is particularly useful for monitoring logs.

Scroll through a file
less file.txt
or:
more file.txt

In less:

↑ / ↓       → Move
Space       → Next page
b           → Previous page
q           → Quit
/word       → Search

