7. Introduction to Text Editors

Linux commonly provides terminal-based text editors.
Nano

Open/create a file:
nano file.txt

Useful shortcuts:
Ctrl + O → Save
Ctrl + X → Exit
Ctrl + W → Search
Ctrl + K → Cut line
Ctrl + U → Paste
Vim

Open a file:
vim file.txt

Basic Vim modes:
Normal Mode
     ↓
Press i
     ↓
Insert Mode
     ↓
Press Esc
     ↓
Normal Mode

Save and exit:
:wq

Exit without saving:
:q!

Save:
:w

For beginners, Nano is easier to start with, while knowing basic Vim is useful because it is commonly available on Linux servers.

